jobs.description:
The Executive Vice President (EVP) of Technology is a senior technical leadership role responsible for formulating and executing the technology strategy. This position oversees technical architecture, engineering R&D, technical operations, digital transformation, and major technical initiatives.

Acting as a bridge between corporate strategy, technology strategy, and execution management, the role ensures the technology organization stably and efficiently supports business growth, product innovation, and long-term scalable development.

Core Responsibilities

I. Technology Strategy and Planning
Formulate the enterprise's medium- to long-term technology strategy and development roadmap;
Translate corporate strategic goals into actionable technology execution plans;
Evaluate emerging technologies and their business application value;
Determine priorities for technology investment and R&D;
Provide strategic technology advice to the CEO, CTO, and Board of Directors.

II. Technology Organization Management
Oversee engineering, R&D, architecture, infrastructure, and technical operations teams;
Establish an enterprise-wide technology management framework;
Optimize the technical organizational structure and role definitions;
Develop systems for technical talent cultivation and succession planning;
Manage VPs, Senior Directors, and technical leads.

III. Technology Execution and Delivery
Supervise major technical projects and strategic technology initiatives;
Define milestones and delivery standards for technical projects;
Manage project resources, budgets, and execution risks;
Ensure the timely, high-quality completion of technology initiatives;
Resolve cross-team obstacles hindering technical execution.

IV. Enterprise Technology Architecture
Oversee the evolution of the enterprise's overall technology architecture;
Build scalable, high-performance, and stable technical infrastructure;
Drive system modernization and technology platform upgrades;
Define technical standards and engineering specifications;
Manage technical debt and architectural risks.

V. R&D and Engineering Efficiency
Optimize software R&D and engineering management processes;
Promote Agile, DevOps, and continuous delivery practices;
Enhance R&D productivity and technical delivery efficiency;
Establish metrics for engineering quality and reliability;
Drive the development of automation and engineering tools.

VI. Digitalization and Technology Innovation
Drive enterprise digitalization and technology innovation initiatives;
Evaluate AI, cloud computing, data platforms, and automation technologies;
Facilitate the transition of new technologies from proof-of-concept to practical application;
Establish management mechanisms for technology innovation;
Ensure innovation initiatives deliver measurable business value.

VII. Technology Risk and Security
Oversee major technology risks;
Collaborate with executives such as the CIO and CISO;
Establish mechanisms for system reliability and business continuity;
Drive infrastructure and application security standards;
Manage major technology incidents and recovery efforts.

VIII. Budget and Vendor Management
Develop the annual budget for the technology organization;
Manage technical personnel, infrastructure, and software resources;
Oversee technology vendors and strategic partners;
Optimize technology costs;
Evaluate the ROI of technology investments.

Qualifications

Education
Bachelor’s degree or higher in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Technology, Engineering, or a related field;
MBA, Master’s in Engineering Management, or related Master’s degree preferred.

Work Experience
20+ years of experience in technology, engineering, R&D, or IT management;
15+ years of experience in senior technology leadership;
Experience in roles such as EVP of Technology, CTO, SVP of Engineering, or VP of Technology preferred;
Experience managing large-scale technology organizations or global technology teams;
Experience in enterprise-level technology transformation and scaling.

Core Competencies
Technology Strategy;
Technology Execution;
Enterprise Architecture;
Engineering Leadership;
R&D Management;
Digital Transformation;
AI & Data Strategy;
Cloud Infrastructure;
Technology Operations;
Technology Project Management;
Budget and Resource Management;
Senior Team Leadership.

Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)
Technology strategy execution rate;
On-time completion rate of major technology projects;
Product and system delivery cycle time;
System stability and availability;
Engineering productivity;
Technology cost optimization rate;
Technology project ROI;
Technical debt reduction rate;
Implementation rate of technology innovation projects;
Resolution rate of major technology risks.

Show more

Show less

Seniority level

Executive

Employment type

Full-time

